{# Thomas's words, from his original Music Box page. #}
<p>The Modular Music Box is an audiovisual instrument for exploring harmony and geometry. Generate notes from a library of scales, or build harmonies by stacking musical intervals in cells or in a series. For the inquisitive, an advanced interval and chord ID system called the "Identifier" analyzes the harmony in real-time to tell you exactly what sounds you're creating. With visual controls for glow, trails, and color, The Modular Music Box is a playground for both musical and aesthetic discovery into the complex patterns that emerge from simple music rules.</p>
<p>Structure inspired by <a href="https://www.whitneymusicbox.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jim Bumgardner's "Whitley Music Box"</a>. Harmonic visualization technique based on Schoenberg's pitch class set theory.</p>
